v7: the per-project knowledge base — its two layers, and the create-or-update decision for a feature note

Usage: <BIN> knowledge [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  list       List the base: transverse notes, then one line per feature note
  resolve    Decide whether a feature has a note (`update`) or needs one (`create`, with the path to write); `ambiguous` means several notes are close: read them
  index      Regenerate the knowledge index notes (`_<repo>.md`, `Features/_Features.md`, `_Knowledge.md`) for every documented project. Run it after hand-editing
  path       Print the resolved paths of both layers
  stats      Base-wide health: feature/root-note counts, size, oversized notes, colliding handles, and the adoption count for `files:`
  supersede  Mark a feature note superseded by upserting `status`, `valid_until`, `superseded_by` and optional `supersede_reason` in its frontmatter; never deletes it
  stale      Date every feature note's `files:` against git history, cache the result in `<knowledge_dir>/.aidp-stale.json` and print the report; never fails
  gc         Read-only report on forks, dangling `superseded_by` pointers and notes whose `files:` are all gone. Always exits 0
  help       Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --workspace-root <PATH>
          Workspace to act on instead of the current directory

      --vault <PATH>
          Obsidian vault to use instead of `AIDP_VAULT`, `~/.aidp/config.json` or auto-detection

      --no-vault
          Ignore any vault and keep artefacts in the repo (`.aidp/pipelines/`)

      --no-knowledge
          Leave the compile-time `## Knowledge` block out of the stage prompts

      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format. Each command keeps its own default when omitted

          Possible values:
          - json-compact: One compact JSON document on a single line
          - json-pretty:  One indented JSON document
          - ndjson:       One compact JSON value per line
          - text:         Human-readable text
          - footer:       The one-line cost footer of a report, for `<BIN> cost ticket`; text elsewhere

  -v, --verbose...
          More diagnostics on stderr; repeat for more (`-vv`)

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
